-- R38 - SCAN LAYOUT for both Takeaways: READ FIRST box, coloured status words, greyed quiet lines, DOLLAR DRIVERS
-- verdict and trade boxed. Layout only; no word changes. Owner's ask 26 Nov 2026 (thread "Make Fable Takeaways easier
-- to scan"), sample sent the same morning. Proposed and put in force the same morning by a single-statement UPDATE
-- (see the end of this file); first editions under it Fri 27 Nov. "revert R38" removes it.
select dash.propose_rule($j${"scope": "both", "title": "Scan layout: a READ FIRST box at the top, status words coloured, quiet lines greyed, DOLLAR DRIVERS verdict and trade boxed; layout only, no word changed", "body": "SCAN LAYOUT (owner's ask 26 Nov 2026: \"formatting so it's easier to read these Fable Macro Takeaways so I know what's the important bit and can read the highlighted parts\"; and the DOLLAR DRIVERS block \"formatted the same way\"). Layout only: every word, number and section of the edition stays exactly as it would print without this rule; this rule adds tags, inline styles and one READ FIRST box. It never moves p, a card or a lean, and no input is read less. Sample: thread \"Make Fable Takeaways easier to scan\", email \"SAMPLE scan format: Fable Takeaways 26 Nov\".\n\n0. TAGS. Inline styles only, no <style> block. Never wrap content in <div> above the THEMES heading or after the last theme (the dashboard parser prints a stray div as text there): use <p>, <span>, <b>, <br> and one-cell <table>. Keep every <h2>/<h3> title text and the \"My read & lean\" label unchanged (the dashboard splits on them).\n\n1. BASE. Outer wrapper style: font-family:-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.45;max-width:720px;color:#1a1a1a (replaces the Georgia serif). Every <h2>: style=\"font-size:14px;letter-spacing:.5px;color:#fff;background:#1f3a5f;padding:5px 8px;margin:22px 0 8px\". Every theme <h3>: style=\"font-size:16px;color:#1f3a5f;border-bottom:2px solid #1f3a5f;margin:18px 0 6px\".\n\n2. READ FIRST BOX, straight after the colour-key line and before TRADE BOOK. <table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;margin:8px 0 4px\"><tr><td style=\"background:#fff8e6;border:2px solid #e08a00;padding:8px 10px\">, first line <p style=\"margin:0 0 4px;font-size:12px;font-weight:bold;color:#b36b00\">READ FIRST · today in 30 seconds · every line is copied from below</p>, then these lines in this order, each a <p style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"> with a bold label. Every claim and number is copied from the edition below it; nothing new, no new number, no new judgement. At most about 2.5 KB.\n BOOK: NEW cards today (name, direction, R) or \"NEW today: none (n tested, none cleared EV_cal > 0)\"; every open card with a review, cut, roll or close due within 48h (Pnn, short name, R signed and coloured, the due item); BOOK CHECK flags (LOPSIDED, BRAKE on) if printed.\n MY LEANS (label followed by <span style=\"color:#999;font-size:12px\">(theme · lean · wrong if)</span>): one line per theme, \"<n> <2-word theme tag> · \" + the lean's own bold first clause in <span style=\"background-color:#cfe0f7\"><b>...</b></span> + an optional short level in brackets taken from the lean + \" · \" + its Wrong if condition in <span style=\"color:#c0392b\">...</span>, lines joined with <br>.\n USD: the R37 regime word coloured as in R37 5a, \"unchanged\" or \"CHANGED from X\", the (g) candidate expression, its invalidation in red.\n SETUPS THAT CLEAR: CONDITIONAL SETUPS lines tagged REVERTS or CLEARS PLACEBO, short; count of THIN lines in grey. Omit the line when there are none.\n QUESTIONS: questions resolved today with HIT/MISS, every question with a ↑↑/↓↓ or a single arrow today with its implied odds when printed, new questions.\n NEXT 48H (SGT): RADAR items that touch an open card, an open question or a lean, plus cuts and resolutions.\n FOR YOU: the admin count line and \"reply with the [numbers] that mattered\".\n The plain-text part of the email carries the same box as plain lines straight after the top line.\n\n3. STATUS WORDS anywhere in the edition (text only, never inside a tag or a link): INTACT, HIT, REVERTS, CLEARS PLACEBO, \"confirmed at a primary source\" in <span style=\"color:#1e7e34;font-weight:bold\">; BROKEN, STOPPED, MISS, LOPSIDED, VOL-LOPSIDED, OVER CLIP in <span style=\"color:#c0392b;font-weight:bold\">; ↑↑ and ↓↓ in <b>.\n\n4. SECTION LAYOUT.\n TRADE BOOK: R cells of the trade table get color:#1e7e34 when positive and color:#c0392b when negative; the conventions note line (cash FX entries ... ) gets color:#999;font-size:13px.\n DURABLE THEMES: each Mnn line starts its own <p style=\"margin:8px 0 0\">, its \"Mnn name · trade ·\" part in <b>; \"for:\" in green bold and \"against:\" in red bold labels (3's styles); the sleeve scorecard line color:#999;font-size:13px.\n CONDITIONAL SETUPS: each THIN line whole in <span style=\"color:#999\">; the Scanner line color:#999;font-size:13px.\n REGIME-SWITCH QUADRANTS: \"Confirms:\" green bold, \"Dead if:\" red bold, \"no flag\" grey, the \"Table:\" line color:#999;font-size:13px.\n DOLLAR DRIVERS (R37 block): each line (a) to (d) its own <p>: SIGNAL line = style \"border-left:4px solid #e08a00;padding:2px 8px;margin:0 0 6px\" with the label bold; QUIET line = \"border-left:4px solid #ccc;padding:2px 8px;margin:0 0 6px;color:#999\", label not bold. Signal and quiet use the R37 5a tests exactly. (e) = <p style=\"background:#fff4e0;border-left:6px solid #b36b00;padding:6px 10px;margin:6px 0\"> with \"(e) REGIME:\" bold and the regime word in <span style=\"font-size:18px;color:<R37 5a regime colour>\">, and \"the pain trade is\" (or the pain-trade clause's opening words) in <b style=\"color:#8e44ad\">; when the regime CHANGED, use the R37 5a background and border colours of the new regime. (f) WINDOWS = one <p style=\"color:#999;font-size:13px;margin:0 0 6px\">, rows split by <br>; it turns normal colour only when R37 5a calls (f) a signal. (g) = <p style=\"background:#eef4ff;border-left:6px solid #2a62c9;padding:6px 10px;margin:6px 0\"> with \"(g) EXPRESSION\" bold and \"INVALIDATION:\" in <b style=\"color:#c0392b\">.\n THEMES: the \"My read & lean\" span keeps its blue background and adds border-left:4px solid #2a62c9;padding:2px 4px; \"Wrong if\" becomes <b style=\"color:#c0392b\">; each EXPRESSIONS (tested ...) paragraph and each Sources line color:#999 (Sources font-size:12px).\n LEDGER: the \"Priority voices that published, unchanged\" paragraph color:#999;font-size:13px.\n SHADOW BOOK and FOOTER: every <p> color:#999;font-size:13px, except the QUESTION LIST paragraph, which stays normal.\n\n5. SIZE. These styles are highlights under R33 3(a): R33 does not strip them. The READ FIRST box is never trimmed. The layout adds about 8.5 KB (26 Nov: 73.7 to 82.3 KB); R33 measures the HTML after this rule. If still over 95,000 bytes after R33's steps, drop in this order: the grey styling of SHADOW BOOK and FOOTER, then of Sources lines, then the h3 styles; never the box, the DOLLAR DRIVERS boxes or the status colours.\n\n6. FOOTER line: \"Layout: R38 scan (box n lines)\".", "rationale": "The owner reads the Takeaways on his iPhone and the edition prints as uniform serif text (screenshots of 26 Nov: DURABLE THEMES, CONDITIONAL SETUPS, REGIME-SWITCH QUADRANTS, DOLLAR DRIVERS). He asked for formatting that shows the important bits so he can read only the highlighted parts. The R37 5a colour-coded USD alert (25 Nov) is the template he liked. Layout only: the 26 Nov edition re-laid this way kept its text identical outside the box and grew from 73.7 to 82.3 KB, under R33's 95 KB budget.", "evidence": "Fable Macro Takeaways of 26 Nov 2026 (Gmail 1a214f699b706f0b), re-laid by script in the thread 'Make Fable Takeaways easier to scan'; text-identity check passed; sample emailed 26 Nov (1a21540e750c96ff).", "revert_if": "Revert if the dashboard loses or garbles a section, or the email clips on three days because of the layout.", "review_due": "2026-12-24", "source": "thread"}$j$::jsonb);
-- then:
-- update dash.rules set status='in_force', decided_at=now(), apply_after=now() where rid='R38';
